-- ################ V256__help_doc_semantic_anchor_gaps.sql ################
-- Help chapters closing the semantic anchor gaps found by the menu help audit.
-- Why: after every multi-chapter leaf got its own anchor, the audit compared what each
-- landing chapter actually explains against what its page does. Ten leaves landed on
-- chapters that never describe their page (prompt templates, training samples, plugins,
-- API tokens, roles, users, executor pools, summary report, statistics report, report
-- center, coverage matrix) and the credential vault had no chapter at all in its domain.
-- Each new chapter follows the four-section page contract (what this page does /
-- how to use / what the system does behind it / common questions).
-- Discipline: bodies carry zero table names / config keys / feature codes; idempotent
-- via ON CONFLICT (domain_code, sort_no) DO UPDATE. Mirrors the V252 pattern.
-- Usage: docker exec -i testpike-postgres psql -U testpike -d testpike -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -f - < this file

